            <ArticleTitle>Primary cardiac paraganglioma with dual coronary blood supply presenting with angina chest pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e278-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary cardiac paraganglioma (pheochromocytoma) is very rare, constituting only 1% of cardiac tumours. A case of a 44-year-old woman presenting with angina chest pain and a tumour with dual blood supply from both the right and left coronary arteries is reported.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
